{{Quote|Do you know everyone here?''"<br />"''Of course. We're all like family.|[[Wrecker]] and Shep Hazard|<ref name="Pabu" />}}
'''Pabu island''',<ref name="Insider">{{InsiderCite|228|Star Wars: The Bad Batch Season Three Companion|''Star Wars: The Bad Batch'' Season Three Companion}}</ref> also simply known as '''Pabu''', was a remote island located on the tropical [[planet]] [[Pabu|of the same name]]. It was led by its [[mayor]], [[Shep Hazard]], and its inhabitants were mostly [[refugee]]s from the [[Clone Wars]]. Although it had limited resources, Pabu provided a friendly atmosphere for refugees that was free of the presence of the [[Galactic Empire]]. [[Phee Genoa]] regarded it as her "home away from home."<ref name="Pabu" />

The island experienced [[Tsunami|sea surges]] on occasion. As such, a large wall was built around [[Upper Pabu]] to protect it. However, after [[Standard year|years]], Pabu expanded into [[Lower Pabu]] as more inhabitants arrived.<ref name="Pabu" />

Upper Pabu featured the [[Archium]], which stored rescued artifacts from around [[the galaxy]]. It also housed the early warning system, which was used to alert the residents of a sea surge. Just outside the Archium was a large landing pad at the very top of the island.<ref name="Pabu" />

At some point, there had not been a major sea surge in almost thirty years. However, that year, the island experienced a series of tremors, which led to a large surge. The surge damaged most of Lower Pabu; however, all of the residents escaped to the safety of Upper Pabu with the help of [[Clone Force 99]].<ref name="Pabu" />

Genoa and Clone Force 99 later attempted to build up the funds needed to restore Pabu. After a failed heist on [[Hosnian Prime]], Tech and Genoa managed to access and siphon exorbitant amounts of money from [[Cellia Moten]]'s accounts, both legal and otherwise, during their encounter on [[Tryth]]. The amount was enough to rebuild Pabu twice over.<ref>''[[Sanctuary: A Bad Batch Novel]]''</ref>

Although Pabu was remote, Clone Force 99 was discovered there on multiple occasions.<ref name="Harbinger">{{TBB|The Harbinger}}</ref><ref name="PoNR">{{TBB|Point of No Return (The Bad Batch)}}</ref> The [[Force-Sensitive Outcast]] [[Asajj Ventress]] found them there, wanting to test [[Omega]]'s ability to [[Force-sensitive|connect]] with [[the Force]].<ref name="Harbinger" /> Later, the [[clone assassin]] [[CX-2]] tracked the [[Cloning|clones]] to Pabu after stealing data from the Genoa's [[starship]], the ''[[Providence]]'', and destroyed their ship, the ''[[Marauder (Omicron-class)|Marauder]]''. An Imperial [[division]] soon arrived to capture Omega, and, after laying waste to parts of the island community, captured the young clone and departed.<ref name="PoNR" />

Following the [[Skirmish on Wayland|fall]] of [[Tantiss Base]], Pabu would cordially play host to all the liberated clone prisoners. Clone Force 99, with the exception of [[Echo]], would permanently settle on Pabu.<ref name="Cavalry>"{{TBB|The Cavalry Has Arrived}}</ref>

At some point between 4 and 2 BBY, Omega decided to depart Pabu to join the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] as a pilot.<ref name="Cavalry" />

